  "problem": "Some researchers want to test the belief that teenagers who play an instrument are more likely to be good at math. They collect data on a large sample of teenagers that play an instrument.\n\n- $30%$ of teenagers play piano, and $50%$ of those teenagers are good at mathematics.\n\n- $20%$ of teenagers play violin, and $60%$ of those teenagers are good at mathematics.\n\n- $50%$ of teenagers play other instruments, and $47%$ of those teenagers are good at mathematics.\n\nIf $10%$ of teenagers started to play music before $6$ years old, and $58%$ of teenagers who started to play before $6$ years old are good at math, what is the probability that a randomly chosen teenager that is good at math started to play music before $6$ years old? Round your answer to $3$ decimal places.",
